                        "glosses": [
                            "The place where a hibernating animal shelters for the winter."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd19b79f-cb9d-4270-8b4a-0d72c0301e75",
                                "sense_id": "d88c0793-cd23-32b4-82b0-bf4e5ed5ab12",
                                "text": "Aeolus Cave, which is set into a wooded hillside in Dorset, Vermont, is believed to be the largest bat hibernaculum in New England; it is estimated that before white-nose hit, nearly three hundred thousand bats—some from as far away as Ontario and Rhode Island—came there to spend the winter."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0e5b07c-437b-43bd-97e5-622908d7c53d",
                                "sense_id": "d88c0793-cd23-32b4-82b0-bf4e5ed5ab12",
                                "text": "In winter, NLEBs use caves and mines as hibernacula.⁹⁴ Suitable habitat for the NLEB is present within the Proposed Route."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c3836f19-6a45-3cff-b785-3f404c7eb72d",
                        "entry_id": "624381c4-e905-3b42-8ea8-4dd1f231cea6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A bud, case, or protective covering that a plant uses to survive the challenging environmental conditions during a dormancy period."
                        ],
